INSERT INTO quizzes (title, description, level, time_limit, status, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('The attraction of Ferris wheels', 'Read the following text and choose the correct answer for each gap [1] - [9]:\n\nWhen did you last see a Ferris wheel? Sometimes called observation wheels, they’re becoming fixtures in our cityscapes. It seems that any city that wants to ensure [1] attractions are on show to the world must have a beautifully designed Ferris wheel. [2] these wheels are usually intended to be temporary structures, more often than not they end [3] staying for a number of reasons, not least because they become so highly thought [4] by residents and visitors.\n\nSo why do cities want them? There’s very [5] doubt that they create a novel focus, but there are several other reasons. They may be used [6] symbols of resurgence or a modern complement to the usual historic attractions tourists visit. They’re also cheaper and quicker to build than most other major landmarks. Finally, seeing the success they’ve [7] in many places, cities may feel [8] sense of competition and be driven [9] build bigger and better versions.', 'B2', 540, 'PUBLISHED', NOW(), NOW());
