INSERT INTO quizzes (title, description, level, time_limit, status, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('Constantly moving!', 'Read the following text and choose the correct answer for each gap [1] - [11]:\n\nDo you know any fidgets, people who are [1] still as they are constantly tapping their foot or drumming their fingers? They may irritate colleagues and annoy family members [2] these movements, but researchers have discovered that serial fidgets can burn up to ten times as many calories a day as [3] of us who keep still.\n\nAlthough planned physical activity tends to be the focus [4] current health advice, this is not the [5] way we can burn calories. Every time we move, our bodies require energy – the greater the exercise, the more calories we burn off. However, [6] this research suggests is that [7] tiny exercises done often enough can have as big an effect as rigorous exercises done less frequently.\n\nExactly [8] some people fidget and others don’t is unclear, but some factors such as being anxious or being [9] stress can make individuals more prone [10] fidgeting. It also seems that children fidget more than adults; it is a common misconception that this is brought [11] by boredom, but in fact, it is because they need more exercise.', 'B2', 660, 'PUBLISHED', NOW(), NOW());
