INSERT INTO quizzes (title, description, level, time_limit, status, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('Online passwords – what everyone should know', 'Read the following text and choose the correct answer for each gap [1] - [9]:\n\nWhen [1] comes to online security, we all know what we ought to do: choose a different, random set of letters and numbers for every email account, shopping site or bank account.  But hardly [2] does this, because memorising them all is impossible.  So we use the same familiar words for every site, [3]  a pet’s name or, even worse, the word ‘password’, occasionally remembering to replace the letter O with a zero, or choosing to [4] use of a capital letter.\n\nEven if we opt [5] a random group of letters such as ‘fpqzy’, there is now software available which can make a thousand guesses per second, enabling a hacker to get to your password in just under four hours.\n\nInterestingly, [6] increasing your password to twenty random letters, you increase a hacker’s guessing time to 6.5 thousand trillion centuries.  The problem is that you would [7] no chance of ever remembering those 20 letters.  The solution, apparently, is to come [8] with three or four short, unrelated words and work [9] a way to remember them.  Easy!', 'B2', 540, 'PUBLISHED', NOW(), NOW());
