INSERT INTO quizzes (title, description, level, time_limit, status, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('Acoustic Levitation', 'Read the following text and choose the correct answer for each gap [1] - [9]:\n\nFloating coffee beans, dancing water droplets – you’d be forgiven [1] thinking you were seeing things on finding [2] faced with these phenomena. But now scientists have discovered how to manipulate objects by using high-frequency sound waves, which allow them to resist the force of gravity. This has opened up the possibility of carrying [3] delicate  experiments and even creating new materials.\n\nAcoustic levitation was first developed in the 1980s, but [4] now, scientists could only hold an object in place or rotate it [5] the spot. Now researchers are able to move objects from place to place, and handle several at [6] .\n\nThe technique could be used to move hazardous chemicals, but there are also far [7] exciting possibilities. Super-cooled liquid metals, which start freezing as [8] as they’re put in a container, could be levitated and would then remain [9] liquids, and could be combined to form entirely new materials. In theory the technique could even be used to levitate animals or people – although this is not possible at present.', 'C1', 540, 'PUBLISHED', NOW(), NOW());
