INSERT INTO quizzes (title, description, level, time_limit, status, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('Video Games and Life', 'Read the following text and choose the correct answer for each gap [1] - [10]:\n\nVideo games are often perceived as being nothing [1] real life. [2] closer examination, however, they often prove to bear a remarkable resemblance to some features of everyday life. For example, almost [3] exception they reward hard work. [4] when you have repeated the same activity many times do you progress to the next level. This is a useful, [5] somewhat mechanical, way of thinking about life: decide on a goal and keep working hard [6] it is achieved.\n\nIt is a metaphor that is [7] from perfect, however. In video games everyone starts out equal whereas it [8] without saying that in life we aren’t all born with the same skills and opportunities.\n\nCritics should also applaud the fact that on the [9] games tend to emphasise personal responsibility. Playing a game over and over allows players to consider the many possible consequences of their decisions. But [10] as we may wish life sometimes gave us the opportunity to do this, the reality is we don’t get many second chances.', 'C1', 600, 'PUBLISHED', NOW(), NOW());
