INSERT INTO quizzes (title, description, level, time_limit, status, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('Commotion in the ocean', 'Read the following text and choose the correct answer for each gap [1] - [9]:\n\nMarine animals have recently been found stranded on beaches [1] Hawaii to the Canary Islands, in locations where noisy industrial activity was [2] place nearby. Some scientists have [3] forward the idea that human-made noise may upset and confuse marine life. And it’s not just mammals that are [4] risk; even fish might be affected by discordant sounds they are simply not used to.\n\nMany human-made sounds are low frequency and within the hearing range of most aquatic animals. What’s [5] , low-pitched sound can travel over considerable distances underwater, which is [6] many of these animals favour it for communication. But this means that noisy industrial activity can disorientate them and change their behaviour. \n\nThe problem is determining what, if [7] , we can do about this. It is [8] from easy to establish which sounds underwater creatures can hear, and even, in some [9] , whether they can hear at all. However, there is no question that the more we discover, the more harmoniously we can coexist with marine life.', 'C1', 540, 'PUBLISHED', NOW(), NOW());
